      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "Land and execute a runnable Python script that (1) symbolically verifies the exact soliton ansatz against the chosen NLSE sign convention (iψ_t + (1/2)ψ_xx + |ψ|²ψ = 0 → sech profile), (2) implements a split-step Fourier propagator with de-aliasing, (3) implements a conservative Crank–Nicolson finite-difference cross-check with predictor–corrector nonlinear solve, (4) computes L2-norm error versus the exact moving soliton at t = 0, 2, 5, 10 together with discrete mass, energy, and momentum and their relative drifts, (5) runs a mesh-refinement loop (Δx, Δt)/2 to measure convergence order, and (6) prints concrete numbers. If any tolerance (L2 < 1e-6, energy drift < 1e-8, momentum drift < 1e-7) is missed, the script reports the actual values and the retained assumptions in an explicit incompleteness block rather than asserting compliance."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "expected_prediction",
      "value": "The script will output concrete L2 errors at t = 0, 2, 5, 10 for both methods, relative drifts of discrete mass/energy/momentum, and measured convergence orders from the refinement study. Split-step Fourier with sufficient resolution should achieve L2 ≲ 1e-6 and energy/momentum drifts near machine-precision levels for the coarse mesh; Crank–Nicolson should show second-order convergence in Δt and Δx. If the coarse mesh fails the t = 10 phase/position tolerance, the refinement study will reveal the required (Δx, Δt) and the exact failure point will be reported honestly."
    },
